<!--
  The configuration of com.kisscodesystems.KissAs3Fw.config.ComponentsConfig.

  This file holds every configurable value of that class with the value the class
  itself codes as its default, so it is the full list of the keys that can be used.
  Deleting a line from here is safe: a key that is missing keeps the default coded
  into the class, so an empty config element is valid too.

  The key of a value element is the name of the protected variable of that class.
  A color can be given in the 0xRRGGBB, the #RRGGBB or the plain decimal form, and
  a boolean can be given as true, false, 1 or 0. A value is taken exactly as it is
  written, so a leading or a trailing space is kept.

  The blur filters and the text drop shadow arrays cannot be configured from here,
  those are coded into the class.

  This is the configuration of the framework itself. An application based on KissAs3Fw
  keeps its own values in its own xml and binds that xml with a small class extending
  ComponentsConfig: that class embeds its xml and overrides readValuesFromConfigXml to call
  the super and then applyConfigXml with it. See ComponentsConfigMusic of KissAs3Mp.
  So the values of an application live in an xml, only the binding is a class.
-->
